      "hints": [
        "Integrate: $f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}(3x-1)^{2/3} + c$.",
        "Substitute $(3,1) \\implies 1 = 2 + c \\implies c = -1$.",
        "At $x = 0$, $y = \\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2/3} - 1 = \\frac{1}{2} - 1 = -\\frac{1}{2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $f'(x) = (3x - 1)^{-1/3}$ using the reverse chain rule:\n$$f(x) = \\int (3x - 1)^{-1/3}\\,dx = \\frac{(3x - 1)^{2/3}}{\\frac{2}{3} \\times 3} + c = \\frac{1}{2}(3x - 1)^{2/3} + c$$",
        "Substitute the coordinates of point $A(3, 1)$ to find the integration constant $c$:\n$$1 = \\frac{1}{2}(3(3) - 1)^{2/3} + c = \\frac{1}{2}(8^{2/3}) + c = \\frac{1}{2}(4) + c = 2 + c \\implies c = -1$$\n$$f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}(3x - 1)^{2/3} - 1$$",
        "Find the $y$-coordinate of $B$ by evaluating at $x = 0$:\n$$y_B = \\frac{1}{2}(3(0) - 1)^{2/3} - 1 = \\frac{1}{2}((-1)^2)^{1/3} - 1 = \\frac{1}{2}(1) - 1 = -\\frac{1}{2}$$"
      ],
